-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>Signing in and creating an account</h2>
+    <p>Both forms ask only for a username and password. You can choose a username that does not identify you; an email address, real name, phone number, and date of birth are not requested.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit a form, your username and password are sent over HTTPS to the authentication service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, hosted on Google Cloud. Sign-in uses this service to check your credentials; sign-up uses it to create an account. Like other network services, it also receives connection information such as your IP address.</p>
+    <p>The forms omit cookies and referrer information from these requests, do not intentionally cache the requests, and do not save credentials or authentication tokens in browser storage. The password field is cleared after each submission attempt. Your browser or password manager may separately offer to remember credentials under your own settings.</p>
+    <p>This website's source does not establish the authentication service's storage, retention, or deletion practices. Those practices need to be confirmed with the service operator; clearing the form does not delete an account or data held by that service.</p>
+
+    <h2>Page resources and tracking</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics or advertising scripts or request remote fonts. No optional tracking consent is required for those disabled resources. The site uses a no-referrer policy to prevent its page address being sent with outgoing requests.</p>
+    <p>Some editorial images and links use external services. When an external resource loads, or you follow a link, that provider receives connection information such as your IP address and handles it under its own policies.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading list and other cookies</h2>
+    <p>Saving an article uses a server-side reading list and a session cookie so the site can retrieve that list on later requests. Simply visiting a page does not initialize a reading list. Clearing your site's cookies removes your browser's connection to that session; it does not by itself delete server-side data.</p>
+    <p>Some interactive articles contain their own scripts and may set feature-specific cookies. The disabled analytics and advertising scripts are not needed to read articles or use the account forms.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
